Why this patch exists
=====================

`ses/dist/ses.cjs` wraps its whole body in `(functors => options => { 'use strict'; … })`,
and its own `assert-sloppy-mode.js` throws when `this` in a receiverless call is not
`undefined` — the strict-mode value. Node honours the directive; bun's transpiler drops it,
so `getThis()` returns `globalThis` and SES refuses to initialise. Nothing that reaches
`@usecannon/builder` can then load under `bun test`, which is every `hardhat.config.ts` in
this repository. One top-level `'use strict';` restores the directive at a scope bun keeps.

`ses@2.3.0` fails the same way, so this is not waiting on a version bump. The longer
explanation, including why the fork's cannon packages make this unavoidable, is in
`pnpm-workspace.yaml` beside the `patchedDependencies` entry that applies this file.

When to drop it
---------------

When bun preserves the directive — but note there is **nothing to watch upstream today**.
The class has been reported twice and both reports are closed as completed:

  https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/5673  ("use strict" doesn't work; bun 1.0, 2023-09)
  https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/8597  ("use strict" ignored when global "this" is
                                               used; bun 1.0.25, 2024-01)

Neither is this exact reproduction and both predate the behaviour measured here on bun
1.3.14 (2026-09), so they are the closest prior art rather than a tracking issue. Anyone
retiring this patch should re-run the check rather than wait for a notification: delete the
patch, `pnpm install`, and run any package's `bun test` — if `hardhat.config.ts` loads, bun
has fixed it. Filing a fresh issue with that reproduction would give this a link to watch.

